On 2007-02-01, sevillad@gmail.com wrote:
> Hi,
>
> I've been playing for a few days and I've finally come to a situation
> where I've accumulated a lot of junk. The problem is not the weight,
> but the quantity; I have repeated potions, darts, and other stuff,
> with separate letters, so I can't pick up anything else. Is there a
> way to stack similar objects? (#adjust swaps letters instead, I
> haven't seen any other command).
>
> Also, sometimes things are stacked automatically (I have one pile with
> 3 darts and another one with 11).

Items that don't stack automatically won't stack at all[1]. This is because
they are not actually identical (your darts may have blesses, curses and
enchantments that you don't know about making them different). You can try
to merge item stacks by identifying them and adjusting their properties
(for example, a wand of cancellation zeros most discerning properties so
items treated with this can stack), but this is only worthwile for missile
stacks.

The way to pick up more items than there are inventory slots is to use a
sack. You can have arbitrarily many items that way.

>                                   I don't know how to drop single
> items (or money for that matter), is that possible?

Yes. d2$ drops two gold pieces. dn<letter> drops n items from slot
<letter>.

[1] Actually, sometimes #adjusting or dropping and picking up can cause
    some items to stack, but this happens only when a stack of items 
    changed some property to match another one while sitting in your 
    inventory.
